es are NOT swept in), so an over-broad path fragment fails loudly.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Goal: 'reduce the macOS cell to the tests whose behaviour genuinely differs'; motivation is runtime (~2140s -> target).","The new guard only asserts a representative set of files COLLECT under the marker ('collect under the marker, so pattern drift fails loudly rather than silently emptying') — it guards the empty direction, not the over-broad direction.","No AC bounds the subset size or asserts it is materially smaller than the full default suite."],"finding":"The plan's core goal is runtime reduction, but none of the acceptance criteria prove the macOS subset is actually SMALLER/bounded than the full suite. If a path fragment in _PLATFORM_COMPAT_PATH_FRAGMENTS is over-broad (e.g. matches many unrelated files), the macOS cell stays large and the latency win evaporates — yet every AC (non-empty collection, representative files collect, Ubuntu unchanged, parity green) still passes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1cb17c8217d5ca20","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / Testing","norm_id":"n1454a8812c2e7587","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the parity/guard test to assert both directions: representative platform files collect under the marker AND a representative non-platform-sensitive file does NOT, or assert the marked count stays under an explicit ceiling.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_veri